\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Illustration of two independent engagements in an $e=\sqrt  {3}/2$ elliptical orbit. At perihelion, a 2-red-on-3-blue engagement unfolds, while at aphelion, a 3-red-on-2-blue encounter occurs. These engagements are causally disconnected—separated by vast distances and hours of orbital evolution. No immediate interaction or synchronization is required, exemplifying the concept of causal bubbles in PDES. Only when orbital dynamics bring these regions into proximity does synchronization become necessary.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
